Topology version 0.01
=====================

Draw what you have, from the git repositories that describe it.  This is
the Perl half of Topology: the command line (topology), the graph API
(topology serve), and the modules they use.  The browser half lives in
www/ at the top of the source tree.

INSTALLATION

To install this module type the following:

   perl Makefile.PL
   make
   make test
   make install

DEPENDENCIES

This module requires perl 5.36 or later and these other modules:

  Feature::Compat::Class   (no further needs on perl 5.42 or later)
  Future
  IO::Async, Future::AsyncAwait   (only for "topology serve")

The Debian packages carry a perl 5.44.0 built for Topology with all of
them vendored in, under /opt/topology/perl; see ../../RECIPE.org.

READING THE CODE

doc/CLASSIC-BRIDGE.pod maps perl's new class syntax onto the
package-and-bless Perl many of us learned first.

